2
00:00:03,513 --> 00:00:03,514

3
00:00:04,136 --> 00:00:05,697
<i>Ah, Christmas.</i>

4
00:00:05,760 --> 00:00:07,897
<i>It's a regular feast
for the senses.</i>

5
00:00:08,000 --> 00:00:11,000
<i>The smells, the sights,
the sounds...</i>

6
00:00:11,113 --> 00:00:13,879
If that's those
charity wrapping paper kids again,

7
00:00:13,968 --> 00:00:16,560
they already hit us twice. They
keep changing hats and scarves,

8
00:00:16,697 --> 00:00:18,672
but I recognize 'em.
It's my parents.

9
00:00:18,777 --> 00:00:21,521
Guys!
Grandma and grandpa are here!

10
00:00:21,631 --> 00:00:22,929
What? Now?

11
00:00:23,009 --> 00:00:24,520
I thought they weren't coming
till Christmas.

12
00:00:24,601 --> 00:00:26,497
Mike, don't look surprised.
I told you about this.

13
00:00:26,576 --> 00:00:28,520
That was my mom.

14
00:00:28,592 --> 00:00:30,424
My parents are coming
a week early for Christmas.

15
00:00:30,553 --> 00:00:33,449
They'll be staying for 12 days.
That's cool with you, right?

16
00:00:33,545 --> 00:00:35,113
Yes, yes, yes, yes!

17
00:00:37,153 --> 00:00:39,128
You purposely told me
during a Colts game.

18
00:00:39,256 --> 00:00:41,632
All I know is that I heard "yes."

19
00:00:41,713 --> 00:00:43,528
Frankie, 12 days?

20
00:00:43,656 --> 00:00:45,601
Mike, I gotta let 'em in.

21
00:00:45,696 --> 00:00:47,561
Yeah, and you can,
in eight days.

22
00:00:47,672 --> 00:00:48,913
Christmas is about family...

23
00:00:48,992 --> 00:00:51,016
Family that's outside right now
getting very suspicious.

24
00:00:51,105 --> 00:00:53,952
Just relax. It's gonna be fun.
12 days?

25
00:00:54,065 --> 00:01:00,225
12 days is too long, Frankie.Nobody's fun
for 12... (Both) Merry Christmas!

26
00:01:03,225 --> 00:01:07,226
There's my big, gorgeous son-in-law!
Mwah! How are ya?

27
00:01:07,304 --> 00:01:08,320
Are we late?

28
00:01:08,417 --> 00:01:11,385
No, no. Uh, you're even earlier
than I expected.

29
00:01:11,464 --> 00:01:14,984
Oh, baby!
Hey! There they are!

30
00:01:15,065 --> 00:01:18,449
Hi, Suzy Q! Oh, look at you. Look at you.
Oh! You've grown. You've grown.

31
00:01:18,568 --> 00:01:22,913
I brought... Fudge.

32
00:01:23,049 --> 00:01:24,377
Awesome!
Thanks, grandma!

33
00:01:24,464 --> 00:01:26,856
Okay, guys, just a couple.
Oh, Frankie.

34
00:01:26,977 --> 00:01:29,552
It's fudge. It's Christmas.

35
00:01:29,633 --> 00:01:31,833
Oh, mom gets out-mommed
by grandma.

36
00:01:31,912 --> 00:01:33,625
Merry Christmas to me.

37
00:01:33,736 --> 00:01:36,745
Hey! Anybody notice
I grew antlers?

38
00:01:36,824 --> 00:01:40,464
I thought they'd be great
for the family skit this year.

39
00:01:40,561 --> 00:01:43,984
Got some for you, too.
Dad, you're finally doing the skit with us?

40
00:01:44,088 --> 00:01:47,289
Oh, don't worry, Sue.
We're gonna get him this year.

41
00:01:47,384 --> 00:01:50,320
Yeah, we've got 12 whole days
to work on ya.

42
00:01:50,417 --> 00:01:53,440
Oh-ho! Hey. Who's countin'?

43
00:01:55,704 --> 00:01:58,457
12 days, and he's already on me
about the skit.

44
00:01:58,568 --> 00:02:00,832
What kind of screwy family
has to do a skit

45
00:02:00,929 --> 00:02:03,849
in the family room every Christmas?
It just feels alien to you

46
00:02:03,952 --> 00:02:07,016
because your family's
not fun. We're fun.

47
00:02:07,113 --> 00:02:10,200
And you're a bunch of
walking corpses who drink.

48
00:02:10,305 --> 00:02:11,338
That's what I'm talking about.

49
00:02:11,416 --> 00:02:13,120
You know,
look at it this way...

50
00:02:13,200 --> 00:02:15,473
After tonight,
there's only 11 more days.

51
00:02:15,601 --> 00:02:17,872
Oh, no.

52
00:02:17,952 --> 00:02:20,097
I only have 11 days
until Christmas?

53
00:02:20,169 --> 00:02:22,824
I still have to shop for
presents and find the stockings

54
00:02:22,936 --> 00:02:25,120
and finish the tree.
Oh, my God!

55
00:02:25,225 --> 00:02:28,401
Oh, and if you go out, I need
a present this big for Sue.

56
00:02:28,496 --> 00:02:30,248
What are you looking for?
It doesn't matter.

57
00:02:30,321 --> 00:02:32,584
I got Axl and Brick something
this big, and it has to take up

58
00:02:32,681 --> 00:02:34,544
the same amount of floor space
so it doesn't look

59
00:02:34,665 --> 00:02:35,649
like we have favorites.

60
00:02:37,160 --> 00:02:38,521
Hey. How's this?

61
00:02:39,769 --> 00:02:40,881
Oh, are you kidding?

62
00:02:40,977 --> 00:02:43,753
We got this stupid shower radio
for Axl last Christmas,

63
00:02:43,848 --> 00:02:45,576
and look.
He didn't even open it.

64
00:02:45,688 --> 00:02:47,369
Good. We'll give it to him
again. He won't remember.

65
00:02:47,473 --> 00:02:48,480
And this...

66
00:02:48,568 --> 00:02:50,656
I spent $20 for rush delivery

67
00:02:50,712 --> 00:02:51,968
so the kids could open it
Christmas morning

68
00:02:52,192 --> 00:02:56,208
only to have them dump it down here
Christmas night. Ugh. You ow what?

69
00:02:56,281 --> 00:02:58,600
Don't even tell me those things.
It makes me kind of mad. Me, too.

70
00:02:58,793 --> 00:03:01,056
I mean, I drive myself nuts
running around

71
00:03:01,136 --> 00:03:02,617
buyin' all this stuff for them,

72
00:03:02,689 --> 00:03:05,585
and for what, Mike? Really, for what?
Didn't you say you were looking for stockings?

73
00:03:05,672 --> 00:03:07,944
Yeah. Ahh.
Here they are, in the Easter box.

74
00:03:08,048 --> 00:03:10,113
What the hell is that?

75
00:03:12,377 --> 00:03:13,592
It's the orange...

76
00:03:13,697 --> 00:03:16,728
The orange I put in their
stocking every year, you know?

77
00:03:16,833 --> 00:03:19,472
'Cause during the depression,
the only thing that my grandma

78
00:03:19,586 --> 00:03:21,761
got in her stocking
was an orange,

79
00:03:21,856 --> 00:03:23,962
but she loved it
and it was enough.

80
00:03:24,048 --> 00:03:26,024
And that's why my mom put it
in my stocking,

81
00:03:26,144 --> 00:03:27,433
we put one in our kids',

82
00:03:27,568 --> 00:03:29,745
'cause I never want them
to forget to appreciate

83
00:03:29,840 --> 00:03:33,248
something as pure and simple
as an orange.

84
00:03:33,384 --> 00:03:35,744
Look, you're always complaining
about how hard Christmas is?

85
00:03:35,857 --> 00:03:39,064
What if we found a way to... to find
the true meaning of Christmas again?

86
00:03:39,192 --> 00:03:41,057
I-I was thinking
spend less money.

87
00:03:41,192 --> 00:03:42,337
But that'd work, too.

88
00:03:42,545 --> 00:03:44,952
♪

89
00:03:45,232 --> 00:03:47,056
Listen, dad and I want to
talk to you about something.

90
00:03:47,209 --> 00:03:50,009
Mm. This can't be good.
Relax.

91
00:03:50,136 --> 00:03:51,464
We're doing a little
thinking about Christmas.

92
00:03:51,569 --> 00:03:53,609
It seems that we don't always
appreciate it the way we should.

93
00:03:53,696 --> 00:03:56,920
Oh, no, we appreciate it.
Mm, we totally appreciate it.

94
00:03:57,016 --> 00:03:58,096
Do you?

95
00:04:00,184 --> 00:04:01,256
Exhibit "a."

96
00:04:02,209 --> 00:04:05,088
Does anybody recognize that?
We'll give you a hint.

97
00:04:05,249 --> 00:04:07,360
<i>One of you had to have it
just last .</i>

98
00:04:07,476 --> 00:04:10,480
Well... it's lame,
so I'll go with Sue.

99
00:04:10,585 --> 00:04:13,272
Ooh! Sorry. We were looking
for "Axl."

100
00:04:13,392 --> 00:04:15,585
The correct answer
is "Axl."

101
00:04:15,712 --> 00:04:19,265
And it's not even opened.
Wow. That is unappreciative.

102
00:04:19,368 --> 00:04:22,001
Huh. That's funny
you should say that, Sue.

103
00:04:22,112 --> 00:04:22,856
Or should I say...

104
00:04:22,961 --> 00:04:24,920
Exhibit "b."

105
00:04:25,072 --> 00:04:28,856
Oh! Thank you!
I've been looking for this.

106
00:04:28,969 --> 00:04:30,217
Been in the middle
of the pool table all year,

107
00:04:30,304 --> 00:04:31,768
right next to...

108
00:04:31,897 --> 00:04:33,864
Exhibit "c"!

109
00:04:34,704 --> 00:04:37,073
A word-a-day calendar?
Well, you know that's not mine.

110
00:04:37,176 --> 00:04:39,664
Brick stopped using it
on January 2nd.

111
00:04:39,785 --> 00:04:42,152
"And coincidentally,
the word is irresponsible."

112
00:04:42,264 --> 00:04:44,362
This is why
your dad and I have decided

113
00:04:44,464 --> 00:04:46,264
to simplify things this year.

114
00:04:46,377 --> 00:04:47,816
<i>What?</i>

115
00:04:47,904 --> 00:04:49,161
Okay.

116
00:04:50,418 --> 00:04:51,249
Guys...

117
00:04:51,353 --> 00:04:54,776
I just feel like we've lost
the meaning of Christmas.

118
00:04:54,864 --> 00:04:56,112
Now grandma and grandpa
are here.

119
00:04:56,216 --> 00:04:58,706
We have 11 more days.
Wouldn't it be great if we,

120
00:04:58,817 --> 00:05:02,528
as a family, could rethink
just doing what we always do

121
00:05:02,625 --> 00:05:05,432
and find a way to reclaim
Christmas... the good parts?

122
00:05:05,528 --> 00:05:07,834
To truly experience the orange.

123
00:05:07,920 --> 00:05:10,256
Oh, my God!

124
00:05:10,392 --> 00:05:11,713
They're not
getting us presents!

125
00:05:11,825 --> 00:05:13,528
What's the orange again?

126
00:05:13,641 --> 00:05:15,449
Is that true? Are you weenying
out on getting us presents?

127
00:05:15,561 --> 00:05:17,488
Calm down. Nobody's weenying
out of anything.

128
00:05:17,648 --> 00:05:20,708
There'll be presents, just maybe not so many.
All 'cause of an orange?

129
00:05:20,941 --> 00:05:23,653
What's the orange? You remember.
From our stockings.

130
00:05:23,748 --> 00:05:25,580
That stupid orange from when
mom used to live on the prairie

131
00:05:25,677 --> 00:05:28,804
and all she got for Christmas was an orange.
Uh, it wasn't frontier days,

132
00:05:28,901 --> 00:05:31,365
it's your great-grandmother
during the depression.

133
00:05:31,485 --> 00:05:34,429
- How old do you think I am? - God,
I don't know. I try not to think about you.

134
00:05:34,524 --> 00:05:38,068
Aah! Axl be quiet, and please
let our pretty young mother

135
00:05:38,132 --> 00:05:40,020
finish telling us
about the presents.

136
00:05:40,124 --> 00:05:41,292
Well, we thought
instead of going crazy

137
00:05:41,372 --> 00:05:42,676
buying piles of crap,

138
00:05:42,781 --> 00:05:44,428
we could give you just
a couple special things

139
00:05:44,525 --> 00:05:46,261
that would really mean
something to you.

140
00:05:46,429 --> 00:05:48,524
Yeah, and if you wanna get
something for each other

141
00:05:48,596 --> 00:05:50,853
or your friends,
you can earn the money.

142
00:05:50,949 --> 00:05:54,228
Or make something homemade,
from the heart.

143
00:05:54,429 --> 00:05:57,237
From the... heart? Where is this
coming from? It's Christmas!

144
00:05:57,357 --> 00:05:59,197
Maybe it wouldn't be so bad...

145
00:05:59,268 --> 00:06:01,749
Thinking of something special
we really want?

146
00:06:01,870 --> 00:06:02,782
Traitor!
Sue!

147
00:06:02,892 --> 00:06:04,380
It's kind of a nice thought.

148
00:06:04,485 --> 00:06:07,084
I know one thing
I would really like

149
00:06:07,198 --> 00:06:08,644
is a new diary.

150
00:06:10,853 --> 00:06:13,221
Oh, my God!
How did you know?

151
00:06:13,325 --> 00:06:15,812
We found it under a sweater
on Brick's train set.

152
00:06:15,990 --> 00:06:17,197
It's exhibit "d."

153
00:06:20,668 --> 00:06:21,788
<i>Well, once they got used
to the idea,</i>

154
00:06:21,916 --> 00:06:24,077
<i>the "simple Christmas" thing
really took off.</i>

155
00:06:24,220 --> 00:06:26,197
<i>I had time to bake cookies
with my mom,</i>

156
00:06:26,357 --> 00:06:28,477
<i>and since Sue wanted to
buy gifts for everyone,</i>

157
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:32,413
<i>she went out the next day and
got herself a job.</i>

158
00:06:33,180 --> 00:06:34,372
Hey!
Sorry!

159
00:06:34,494 --> 00:06:36,653
<i>Even Axl surprised us
and got into the spirit.</i>

160
00:06:36,764 --> 00:06:39,150
So, since we're doing this
lame-o simple thing,

161
00:06:39,269 --> 00:06:41,822
<i>and there's no way I'm
spending my own money on you,</i>

162
00:06:41,932 --> 00:06:45,109
I'm giving you the most awesome
gift of all... the gift of me.

163
00:06:45,246 --> 00:06:47,772
Oh, but no hugging, no touching,
no contact of any kind,

164
00:06:47,861 --> 00:06:49,372
and you've gotta decide within
the next three seconds

165
00:06:49,461 --> 00:06:51,396
or the offer's void.

166
00:06:55,285 --> 00:06:56,173
What?

167
00:06:58,684 --> 00:07:00,140
I want you
to build me an igloo.

168
00:07:00,300 --> 00:07:02,534
Oh, whew. I thought you
were gonna... make me read.

169
00:07:02,668 --> 00:07:05,397
<i>Yep, the simple Christmas
was bringing people together,</i>

170
00:07:05,493 --> 00:07:08,468
<i>even more together than
some people would have hoped.</i>

171
00:07:08,596 --> 00:07:10,069
Heh! There you are!

172
00:07:10,260 --> 00:07:13,061
Hey, did I ever tell you
about my neighbor, Stan?

173
00:07:13,189 --> 00:07:16,405
Found a tumor behind his eyeball
big as a grapefruit.

174
00:07:16,534 --> 00:07:17,724
Big as a grapefruit.

175
00:07:17,821 --> 00:07:19,661
There you are!

176
00:07:21,245 --> 00:07:22,548
Oh, me, too.
I love the quiet.

177
00:07:22,669 --> 00:07:27,253
My favorite part
of being quiet is when

178
00:07:27,366 --> 00:07:28,454
two people get together...

179
00:07:28,580 --> 00:07:29,924
Hey! There you are!

180
00:07:30,052 --> 00:07:32,580
What's that,
snow you're shoveling there?

181
00:07:32,677 --> 00:07:35,420
You know, I knew three guys
died shoveling snow?

182
00:07:35,540 --> 00:07:40,668
♪ Follow me in merry measure ♪

183
00:07:42,159 --> 00:07:44,032
So, what do you think, huh?

184
00:07:44,134 --> 00:07:46,006
I thought we were doing
a second story.

185
00:07:47,776 --> 00:07:49,495
Where's the reading nook?

186
00:07:49,927 --> 00:07:53,527
I was hoping it'd be next to the hearth.
A hearth? Oh, my God.

187
00:07:53,647 --> 00:07:55,087
This is, like, the first thing
I've actually finished

188
00:07:55,191 --> 00:07:57,167
in my entire life, and you
don't even appreciate it?

189
00:07:57,302 --> 00:07:59,967
Not very orange-y of you,
is it, Brick?

190
00:08:00,095 --> 00:08:01,550
I'm gonna go inside
and get something to eat.

191
00:08:01,695 --> 00:08:04,752
If you built the kitchen
I asked for,

192
00:08:04,887 --> 00:08:06,312
you wouldn't have to go in.

193
00:08:12,599 --> 00:08:14,246
Hey, hey, hey, hey.
Axl, what are you doing?

194
00:08:14,335 --> 00:08:16,503
You're getting the floor all wet.
Are you on me, too? 'Cause I'm not

195
00:08:16,607 --> 00:08:18,992
a professional igloo builder.
I'm doing my best. Clean up your mess.

196
00:08:19,102 --> 00:08:22,400
It's just a little snow.
He's a teenager.

197
00:08:22,502 --> 00:08:23,576
That's what they do.

198
00:08:23,686 --> 00:08:26,200
Uh, what was that?
What was what?

199
00:08:26,294 --> 00:08:28,479
This. You waved me off.

200
00:08:28,648 --> 00:08:32,758
Don't be ridiculous, I did not.
Aah! There! You're doing it again!

201
00:08:32,888 --> 00:08:35,631
I'm his mom, and I need him
to clean up his mess.

202
00:08:35,807 --> 00:08:37,166
Okay, fine.

203
00:08:37,280 --> 00:08:41,286
Axl, listen to your mom
and clean up your mess.

204
00:08:42,735 --> 00:08:43,951
I saw that.

205
00:08:44,135 --> 00:08:46,360
What?
You winked. You just winked.

206
00:08:46,454 --> 00:08:48,935
Wh... there was something
in my eye.

207
00:08:49,047 --> 00:08:50,455
No, this is something
in your eye.

208
00:08:50,543 --> 00:08:52,823
This is a wink.

209
00:08:53,414 --> 00:08:54,608
I know what a wink is.
It means,

210
00:08:54,703 --> 00:08:58,015
"don't listen to your mom.
She's crazy." (Gasps) It does not.

211
00:08:58,127 --> 00:09:00,816
Oh, yes, it does. Janet and I
do it about you all the time.

212
00:09:06,816 --> 00:09:10,183
Just wipe up the floor, Axl,
before you leave the kitchen.

213
00:09:10,375 --> 00:09:12,215
You heard your mother.

214
00:09:16,031 --> 00:09:17,847
I'm already up.
I'll just do it.

215
00:09:18,659 --> 00:09:20,535
<i>For seven days,
Mike put up with my dad.</i>

216
00:09:20,758 --> 00:09:23,159
<i>But on the eighth day,
he hid.</i>

217
00:09:33,463 --> 00:09:34,623
There you are!

218
00:09:34,999 --> 00:09:36,134
Yeah! Just checkin' out

219
00:09:36,279 --> 00:09:38,398
the hot water heater.
It's been actin' funny.

220
00:09:38,575 --> 00:09:41,141
Maybe I can help you out.
Hey, did I ever tell you about

221
00:09:41,213 --> 00:09:43,845
the time I met the weatherman,
Storm McMartin?

222
00:09:43,991 --> 00:09:47,054
I mean, he was just walking along the
street like nothing... Oh! Hey, look at...

223
00:09:47,142 --> 00:09:49,399
Here it is. Yep.
That's the problem.

224
00:09:49,486 --> 00:09:51,478
Better go to the hardware store,
get another one of these.

225
00:09:51,582 --> 00:09:54,126
I'd ask you along, but...
Sure, I'll keep you company.

226
00:09:55,718 --> 00:09:58,350
Okay, kids.
What's up, grandma?

227
00:09:58,455 --> 00:10:01,301
Well, your grandpa and I were
chatting on the way down here,

228
00:10:01,430 --> 00:10:04,894
and we thought that we would
give you all a little something

229
00:10:04,959 --> 00:10:07,430
extra...

230
00:10:07,535 --> 00:10:09,399
It's not your Christmas.

231
00:10:09,494 --> 00:10:11,839
It's just... for...

232
00:10:11,941 --> 00:10:13,255
A-fun.

233
00:10:13,630 --> 00:10:15,999
$100! Oh, my God!

234
00:10:16,111 --> 00:10:17,814
Aah!
Grandma, you're the best!

235
00:10:17,903 --> 00:10:20,879
My first Benjamin!

236
00:10:21,013 --> 00:10:23,262
Mom, that's an awful lot
of money.

237
00:10:23,398 --> 00:10:26,071
Oh, well, we can't
take it with us, right?

238
00:10:26,190 --> 00:10:27,335
Whoo-hoo!

239
00:10:27,430 --> 00:10:31,358
I am done spinning arrows. I'm rich!
Wait, wait, guys. Hang on.

240
00:10:31,430 --> 00:10:33,999
Sue, you're making your own
money. Doesn't that feel good?

241
00:10:34,110 --> 00:10:36,319
And, Brick, you were excited
about those coupons

242
00:10:36,407 --> 00:10:38,079
you were making for us.
Let's be honest.

243
00:10:38,182 --> 00:10:40,182
I was never really gonna
honor 'em, anyway.

244
00:10:41,911 --> 00:10:43,247
Mom...
Hmm?

245
00:10:43,367 --> 00:10:47,031
Listen, you didn't know this,
but Mike and I decided

246
00:10:47,087 --> 00:10:48,999
to do a more simple Christmas
this year...

247
00:10:49,151 --> 00:10:50,974
You know, not about stuff
and things, but more about

248
00:10:51,071 --> 00:10:55,622
family and being together. Oh.
I'm sorry. I... I-I didn't know.

249
00:10:55,774 --> 00:10:58,944
Okay, kids! Your mom wants you
to give the money back.

250
00:10:59,072 --> 00:11:02,129
What? Mom! No!
No, mom, I'm not giving this back!

251
00:11:02,241 --> 00:11:04,426
Mom, you can't do this to us!
Come on. You heard her. No money.

252
00:11:04,505 --> 00:11:07,664
No, no, no, no, no. You don't
have to give the money back.

253
00:11:07,809 --> 00:11:09,904
Why don't I put it
in your bank accounts,

254
00:11:10,010 --> 00:11:11,842
where it'll make a nice
half a percent?

255
00:11:12,002 --> 00:11:13,274
Ugh.

256
00:11:14,729 --> 00:11:18,072
♪ Deck the halls
with boughs of holly ♪

257
00:11:18,193 --> 00:11:21,281
♪ da da-da da-da,
da-da da-da ♪

258
00:11:21,576 --> 00:11:24,202
Ah, it feels good to sing.
Not do the skit, tag.

259
00:11:24,354 --> 00:11:25,562
Should we ask for help?

260
00:11:25,689 --> 00:11:29,978
<i>You know what we could do? We could split up.
Excuse me, there... uh... Kevin. Hey, listen,</i>

261
00:11:30,072 --> 00:11:31,977
would you help my son-in-law
out here?

262
00:11:32,065 --> 00:11:36,736
Don't be afraid
to ask for help.

263
00:11:36,834 --> 00:11:38,425
My friend, Cecil Maynard,

264
00:11:38,488 --> 00:11:41,210
wouldn't ask for help... guess
what happened to him? Choking.

265
00:11:41,354 --> 00:11:43,993
Bam! Face first, right in his soup.

266
00:11:44,145 --> 00:11:46,921
Help me, Kevin. Whoa. Never seen one
break like that through normal use.

267
00:11:47,024 --> 00:11:49,418
Unfortunately, we don't have
this part in stock right now,

268
00:11:49,466 --> 00:11:51,817
and we're not gonna get it in
until after the holidays.

269
00:11:51,938 --> 00:11:53,713
Sorry. You're looking at
some cold showers.

270
00:11:53,842 --> 00:11:56,970
I love a cold shower.
You know what? Well...

271
00:11:57,098 --> 00:12:00,065
♪ Fa-la-la, la-la-la,
la-la-la ♪

272
00:12:00,217 --> 00:12:01,850
He just keeps talking, Frankie.

273
00:12:01,945 --> 00:12:03,346
You know how I feel
about talking.

274
00:12:03,434 --> 00:12:05,961
And he won't give up
on that skit.

275
00:12:06,058 --> 00:12:08,169
You really should the skit.
What are you doing?

276
00:12:08,226 --> 00:12:10,497
Oh, Brick ate too much fudge.

277
00:12:10,593 --> 00:12:13,240
The poor kid just crawled behind
the chair like a cat and barfed.

278
00:12:13,345 --> 00:12:15,890
I told my mom to ease up on
the fudge. She wouldn't listen.

279
00:12:16,019 --> 00:12:18,225
Aha! She's gettin' to ya!

280
00:12:18,354 --> 00:12:20,506
12 days startin' to feel
a little long, Frankie?

281
00:12:20,601 --> 00:12:24,593
For your information, this is
the best Christmas of my life.

282
00:12:24,713 --> 00:12:27,816
Ugh!
How much fudge did he eat?

283
00:12:27,977 --> 00:12:30,904
Whatcha got there?

284
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,161
Nothing.

285
00:12:35,258 --> 00:12:38,033
Really? It looks like an igloo.
Does it?

286
00:12:38,129 --> 00:12:40,690
Oh, yeah. Sort of. I-I guess.

287
00:12:43,345 --> 00:12:45,057
Axl! Glossners!

288
00:12:45,240 --> 00:12:46,170
Wh-what happened?

289
00:12:46,273 --> 00:12:48,018
They looked at the igloo
and smiled!

290
00:12:48,090 --> 00:12:50,073
Dude, you left it alone? They're
gonna try and destroy it!

291
00:12:50,169 --> 00:12:52,426
Get a rope, tennis racket,
shovel, bicycle chain,

292
00:12:52,521 --> 00:12:54,811
and a frying pan!
It's all in there!

293
00:12:54,914 --> 00:12:58,601
Good news. Found a replacement
part in Terra Haute.

294
00:12:58,682 --> 00:12:59,922
Tag's on his power walk.

295
00:13:00,017 --> 00:13:01,833
If you wait till he gets back,
he can go with you.

296
00:13:03,793 --> 00:13:05,897
Can't. Store's closing.
Gotta go.

297
00:13:09,032 --> 00:13:10,904
Hi, dad. We're gonna kill
the glossners.

298
00:13:11,010 --> 00:13:11,824
Okay! Have fun!

299
00:13:14,889 --> 00:13:15,568
Ahh.

300
00:13:18,082 --> 00:13:19,185
Oh, come on.

301
00:13:28,825 --> 00:13:30,944
Uhh!

302
00:13:34,009 --> 00:13:34,625
Come on!

303
00:13:40,466 --> 00:13:41,777
Come on!

304
00:13:47,209 --> 00:13:48,360
There you are!
Aah!

305
00:13:48,466 --> 00:13:52,041
(Laughs) Whew.
Thought you were gonna leave without me.

306
00:13:52,185 --> 00:13:53,753
So did I.

307
00:13:59,026 --> 00:14:00,674
It was the night before Christmas,

308
00:14:00,827 --> 00:14:03,650
<i>and mom was in her kerchief,
and I was in my cap,</i>

309
00:14:03,739 --> 00:14:05,435
<i>and the kids were in the igloo</i>

310
00:14:05,523 --> 00:14:07,355
<i>trying to figure out
how to kill the glossners.</i>

311
00:14:07,771 --> 00:14:08,867
Glossners are hiding
in the bushes.

312
00:14:08,987 --> 00:14:11,907
I saw them when grandma took
fudge over to the Donahues.

313
00:14:12,050 --> 00:14:16,546
I used her as a human shield. I'm cold.
I told you we needed a fireplace.

314
00:14:16,666 --> 00:14:18,402
You can't put a fireplace
in an igloo!

315
00:14:18,475 --> 00:14:20,387
The eskimos do it all the time.

316
00:14:20,475 --> 00:14:22,595
Oh, my God, Brick.
Eskimos aren't even real.

317
00:14:22,674 --> 00:14:24,794
They're just in stories
like leprechauns and trolls.

318
00:14:24,882 --> 00:14:27,402
Would you two stop fighting?
Look at us.

319
00:14:27,499 --> 00:14:29,089
We're fighting with each other.

320
00:14:29,187 --> 00:14:30,683
We're fighting
with our neighbors.

321
00:14:30,787 --> 00:14:34,371
Christmas is supposed to be
a time of peace and joy,

322
00:14:34,466 --> 00:14:38,147
good will toward men...
Even Glossners.

323
00:14:38,243 --> 00:14:40,338
Somebody has to make
the first gesture.

324
00:14:40,435 --> 00:14:42,506
I'm going out there!

325
00:14:43,395 --> 00:14:45,129
What are you doing?
Don't, Sue, no!

326
00:14:50,523 --> 00:14:52,858
♪ Lu lu lu lu ♪

327
00:14:52,962 --> 00:14:53,834
♪ lu... ♪

328
00:15:02,626 --> 00:15:04,130
<i>After Sue crawled to safety
under the car,</i>

329
00:15:04,242 --> 00:15:06,411
<i>I called a truce
and sent the Glossners home</i>

330
00:15:06,515 --> 00:15:07,779
<i>and my kids to bed.</i>

331
00:15:07,915 --> 00:15:11,435
<i>After all, it was the eve
of our first simple Christmas,</i>

332
00:15:11,555 --> 00:15:12,987
<i>and it was perfect.</i>

333
00:15:13,427 --> 00:15:15,746
We did it.
We didn't go overboard.

334
00:15:15,899 --> 00:15:17,834
Sue's getting the iPod
she wanted,

335
00:15:17,931 --> 00:15:20,395
Brick's talking globe,
Axl a new amp.

336
00:15:20,499 --> 00:15:23,435
You know what we filled
this house with? Hmm?

337
00:15:23,531 --> 00:15:26,410
Instead of gifts,
we filled it with love.

338
00:15:26,555 --> 00:15:28,179
Does that make you feel good?

339
00:15:28,282 --> 00:15:31,706
Yep. One more day.

340
00:15:32,052 --> 00:15:34,098
♪ Fa-la-la-la,
la-la, la-la ♪

341
00:15:35,219 --> 00:15:37,011
♪ fast away the old year passes,
fa-la-la, la-la, la-la, la-la ♪

342
00:15:38,867 --> 00:15:40,259
What the hell?

343
00:15:40,458 --> 00:15:45,555
No. Those are Santa gifts
Santa? Over there.

344
00:15:45,674 --> 00:15:46,690
I don't know what these are.

345
00:15:49,217 --> 00:15:55,186
From grandma and grandpa.
Can you believe this?

346
00:15:55,305 --> 00:15:56,698
Can you believe that
she would do this?

347
00:15:56,793 --> 00:16:00,202
I told her that we were
doing a simple Christmas!

348
00:16:00,297 --> 00:16:03,553
Okay. Well, she's not
gettin' away with this.

349
00:16:03,706 --> 00:16:06,402
What happened to "be patient"
and "Christmas is about family"?

350
00:16:06,514 --> 00:16:08,897
Oh, screw that.
Look at all these presents!

351
00:16:08,994 --> 00:16:09,898
You know what this is?

352
00:16:09,978 --> 00:16:13,066
This is a big winking
wave-off from my mom.

353
00:16:13,185 --> 00:16:15,914
Yeah, well, I am the mom
in this house,

354
00:16:15,985 --> 00:16:18,234
and what I say goes!
What are you doing?

355
00:16:18,338 --> 00:16:21,227
Gettin' these in the garage
before the kids wake up!

356
00:16:21,284 --> 00:16:23,274
Me on!
Stuff some in a bag.

357
00:16:23,345 --> 00:16:25,034
Ugh.

358
00:16:29,890 --> 00:16:31,872
Mom...

359
00:16:32,233 --> 00:16:35,362
Why are you taking our presents?
Why?

360
00:16:35,506 --> 00:16:37,409
Uh...

361
00:16:38,346 --> 00:16:39,698
See, the thing is, Brick...

362
00:16:39,809 --> 00:16:42,490
Frankie, what on earth
are you doing?

363
00:16:42,609 --> 00:16:45,194
Presents! Sweet!

364
00:16:45,305 --> 00:16:47,409
There's a kazillion
presents over there!

365
00:16:47,545 --> 00:16:49,586
No, no, no! Hey! Hey...

366
00:16:49,673 --> 00:16:51,009
Guys, there's more of them over here!

367
00:16:51,098 --> 00:16:53,394
No...
Take it over there.

368
00:16:53,481 --> 00:16:56,098
Guys, guys! Did anybody look
in their stocking

369
00:16:56,169 --> 00:16:58,754
and find a refreshing treat?

370
00:16:58,906 --> 00:17:02,617
Hey, stop it. Guys, stop!

371
00:17:02,770 --> 00:17:03,546
Stop it!

372
00:17:03,657 --> 00:17:05,754
Frankie, why don't you let 'em
open their presents?

373
00:17:05,842 --> 00:17:09,248
Because I told you we were
doing a simple Christmas!

374
00:17:09,362 --> 00:17:12,474
Well, I didn't think
you meant us, too.

375
00:17:12,585 --> 00:17:15,953
Oh, you knew I meant you, too,
and you ignored me!

376
00:17:16,058 --> 00:17:18,722
You've been winking and waving
at me all over the place

377
00:17:18,818 --> 00:17:21,554
since you got here!
Well, I am sorry, Frankie,

378
00:17:21,633 --> 00:17:24,914
but there is no way I was
participating in that insanity.

379
00:17:25,010 --> 00:17:28,033
A simple Christmas is just
really a lame idea.

380
00:17:28,137 --> 00:17:29,906
I told you not to tell her that.

381
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:33,698
Well, you don't cut back
at Christmas. It's Christmas!

382
00:17:33,817 --> 00:17:35,930
Who are you people?

383
00:17:36,114 --> 00:17:36,889
When I was a kid,

384
00:17:37,003 --> 00:17:40,577
for my allowance, I got one cent
for every year of my life.

385
00:17:40,658 --> 00:17:44,169
That means when I was 12,
I got 12 pennies, mom.

386
00:17:44,298 --> 00:17:45,274
12 pennies!

387
00:17:45,377 --> 00:17:48,178
Well, back then, we were
parents. Now we're grandparents.

388
00:17:48,242 --> 00:17:50,922
We have to be grand.
It's in the title!

389
00:17:51,002 --> 00:17:52,265
There ain't no pockets
in heaven.

390
00:17:52,321 --> 00:17:57,026
Talking globe?!
Thanks, grandma and grandpa!

391
00:17:57,121 --> 00:17:59,194
You got him the talking globe?!

392
00:17:59,298 --> 00:18:03,169
Yes, I did, and I would do it
again! The only good thing

393
00:18:03,275 --> 00:18:05,562
about getting older
is you get to be popular.

394
00:18:05,665 --> 00:18:08,466
If I have to buy
those kids' love, I will.

395
00:18:08,561 --> 00:18:10,650
Let's get that straight
right now.

396
00:18:10,745 --> 00:18:13,266
We were trying
to learn a lesson!

397
00:18:13,345 --> 00:18:15,690
We were all gonna be better people!
Yeah?

398
00:18:15,737 --> 00:18:17,850
Well, I didn't drive 140 miles

399
00:18:17,945 --> 00:18:20,417
to watch my grandkids
learn a lesson.

400
00:18:20,498 --> 00:18:23,745
What, did you read an article
or something?

401
00:18:23,850 --> 00:18:26,433
Relax! Your kids
are gonna be fine!

402
00:18:26,625 --> 00:18:29,658
I just wanted them
to have a heartfelt Christmas,

403
00:18:29,714 --> 00:18:32,162
you know,
to appreciate the orange.

404
00:18:32,273 --> 00:18:34,993
What's the orange?

405
00:18:35,122 --> 00:18:37,986
The orange in the stocking!

406
00:18:38,097 --> 00:18:39,585
Depression?

407
00:18:39,690 --> 00:18:42,465
Your mom got an orange?
She was really grateful?

408
00:18:42,601 --> 00:18:44,474
Oh, God, that?

409
00:18:44,593 --> 00:18:48,097
You get oranges year-round now.
Who cares?

410
00:18:48,202 --> 00:18:50,970
I care! I care!
I care!

411
00:18:53,329 --> 00:18:55,041
She always flips out
at Christmas.

412
00:18:55,179 --> 00:18:57,626
I think she gets too excited.
Oh, no, no, no, no, no.

413
00:18:57,721 --> 00:18:59,466
Don't you look at Mike
like I'm the crazy one.

414
00:18:59,569 --> 00:19:02,226
He is right in there with me.
You're driving him nuts!

415
00:19:02,305 --> 00:19:04,642
He hates it how you follow him
all over the place,

416
00:19:04,761 --> 00:19:07,209
tellin' him all your stories!
He hates it!

417
00:19:07,361 --> 00:19:09,417
He hates it to himself,
but he hates it!

418
00:19:15,794 --> 00:19:18,881
I told you
to give Mike some space.

419
00:19:21,994 --> 00:19:22,994
Hey, crazy.

420
00:19:23,242 --> 00:19:25,617
I'm a horrible,
horrible person.

421
00:19:25,817 --> 00:19:29,217
It's Christmas,
and I yelled at my parents!

422
00:19:29,434 --> 00:19:31,193
Frankie, I told you,

423
00:19:31,369 --> 00:19:34,433
nobody should have their family
in their house for 12 days.

424
00:19:35,345 --> 00:19:36,522
It goes against nature.

425
00:19:37,114 --> 00:19:39,289
It's why animals in the wild
don't come home for Christmas.

426
00:19:40,001 --> 00:19:42,801
You're right. It's too long.

427
00:19:42,938 --> 00:19:46,074
I just wanted everyone to
remember this year as special,

428
00:19:46,178 --> 00:19:47,570
and now
all they're gonna remember

429
00:19:47,689 --> 00:19:50,553
is that I got all grinchy
and tried to steal the presents

430
00:19:50,682 --> 00:19:52,458
and went off on my mom.

431
00:19:52,553 --> 00:19:56,001
They're not gonna remember it for that.
Yes, they will.

432
00:19:56,123 --> 00:19:58,058
No, they won't.How do you know?

433
00:19:58,137 --> 00:20:00,642
'Cause they're gonna remember it
for something else.

434
00:20:01,530 --> 00:20:04,366
♪ Eight maids a-milking ♪
♪ seven swans a-swimmin' ♪

435
00:20:04,502 --> 00:20:06,446
♪ six geese a-layin' ♪

436
00:20:06,701 --> 00:20:09,046
♪ five golden rings ♪

437
00:20:09,534 --> 00:20:12,798
♪ four calling birds ♪
♪ three French hens ♪

438
00:20:12,926 --> 00:20:14,166
♪ two turtledoves ♪

439
00:20:14,310 --> 00:20:17,486
♪ and a partridge
in a pear tree ♪

440
00:20:17,590 --> 00:20:19,798
<i>It turned out to be one
of our best Christmases yet.</i>

441
00:20:19,901 --> 00:20:21,678
<i>Everyone remembered it
as the year</i>

442
00:20:21,750 --> 00:20:24,630
<i>Mike finally did the skit,
and the kids finally learned</i>

443
00:20:24,741 --> 00:20:26,102
<i>to appreciate the oranges.</i>

444
00:20:31,262 --> 00:20:33,582
<i>And as for my parents and me?
We're fine.</i>

445
00:20:33,686 --> 00:20:35,709
<i>'Cause we know that no matter
what gets said,</i>

446
00:20:35,822 --> 00:20:38,270
<i>we love each other,
and after all,</i>

447
00:20:38,398 --> 00:20:41,390
<i>Christmas is about family.
It's as simple as that.</i>

448
00:20:41,749 --> 00:20:46,950
♪ And a partridge
in a pear tree ♪

449
00:20:48,111 --> 00:20:50,001
